  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Coordination Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.        Value chains within agrifood systems (including agricultural production, processing, distribution and storage, and marketing), as well as consumer behaviour are all subject to biophysical, environmental, technological, infrastructural, political, economic, socio-cultural and demographic drivers. The interaction of the various elements of agrifood systems with the drivers and formal and informal structural and individual inequalities influences social welfare outcomes, as well as dietary, economic, livelihood and environment impacts. Women&#x2019;s engagement in agrifood systems may be on worse terms than that of men if women take on part-time, irregular, informal jobs and entrepreneurship in lower-profit segments of agrifood systems to accommodate their high unpaid domestic and care work burden, and significant gender gaps are evident in wages in agricultural and off-farm activities. Proactively supporting vulnerable segments of society, especially rural and youth women to become active change agents in food production will make rural economies more resilient and can help alleviate local and regional environmental challenges. The project can achieve this through support to inclusive gender-responsive policies and incentives and by encouraging private sector and social enterprise investment in female-led agri-businesses, opening new opportunities for markets and decent employment.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: Disbursement data provided is cumulative and covers disbursement made by the project Agency.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To enhance the effectiveness of the Food Systems Integrated Program in catalyzing food systems transformation and generating global environmental benefits, in selected participating countries and globally</narrative>
  </description>
